1
00:00:15,340 --> 00:00:16,440
It's Reo-kun!!

2
00:00:17,160 --> 00:00:17,940
Reo!!

3
00:00:17,940 --> 00:00:20,490
Reo-kun! Look over here!

4
00:00:20,730 --> 00:00:24,020
Mikage-kun's grades are truly impressive!

5
00:00:24,020 --> 00:00:26,960
Yes! There's nothing that kid can't do.

6
00:00:27,890 --> 00:00:31,810
Two hat-tricks in a row! You're amazing, Reo!

7
00:00:31,970 --> 00:00:37,630
...I've always gotten everything I ever wanted.

8
00:00:36,980 --> 00:00:37,630
...But.

9
00:00:42,130 --> 00:00:48,850
...There might be things in this world... that are beyond my reach.

10
00:00:52,560 --> 00:00:54,220
...But I've finally arrived.

11
00:00:55,140 --> 00:00:58,890
...Finally... I get to fight by your side again.

12
00:00:59,830 --> 00:01:01,040
Nagi!

13
00:01:03,440 --> 00:01:06,080
Watch me closely... okay?

14
00:01:07,210 --> 00:01:09,670
...Alright... let's go.

15
00:02:47,500 --> 00:02:48,980
...In that goal.

16
00:02:49,430 --> 00:02:53,990
...First I tricked Karasu into thinking I'd go there, then I stopped and reversed direction.

17
00:02:53,990 --> 00:02:57,570
...Then I slipped through Rin and Otoya's blind spots.

18
00:03:04,110 --> 00:03:05,450
I have a question!

19
00:03:05,710 --> 00:03:09,680
Did you do all of that after thinking it through carefully?!

20
00:03:09,680 --> 00:03:15,170
...No, it was more like reacting while moving and thinking at the same time.

21
00:03:15,730 --> 00:03:22,150
...And in the end, I slipped between Rin and Shidou and scored.

22
00:03:23,720 --> 00:03:25,150
...That's really incredible.

23
00:03:25,150 --> 00:03:28,310
You did all of that back to back in the blink of an eye.

24
00:03:28,310 --> 00:03:33,900
...That's true, but... I feel like this is the first time I've executed something this complex.

25
00:03:33,900 --> 00:03:38,440
...Even I didn't think you'd be the one to score it, Isagi-kun.

26
00:03:38,960 --> 00:03:42,480
I sent the ball in, sure that either Rin-kun or Shidou-kun would score.

27
00:03:42,820 --> 00:03:48,450
I think it's important for you to analyze your goal over and over until you grasp what you did in that moment, Isagi-kun.

28
00:03:48,450 --> 00:03:53,000
Why did you advise me to be instinctive and rely on my reflexes?

29
00:03:55,410 --> 00:03:58,000
For example... do you know stacking block games?

30
00:04:00,570 --> 00:04:05,280
...They're slow at first, so you have time to think about where to place the block.

31
00:04:05,590 --> 00:04:11,190
But as the speed gradually increases, you no longer have time to think, right?

32
00:04:11,890 --> 00:04:17,860
Playing at a pace that matches Rin-kun and Shidou-kun is almost the same difficulty.

33
00:04:19,690 --> 00:04:21,050
...So that's it.

34
00:04:21,050 --> 00:04:23,860
Moving at my usual pace would be this slow.

35
00:04:23,860 --> 00:04:26,360
How do I stack the blocks...?

36
00:04:26,360 --> 00:04:28,910
Which block can I use right now...?

37
00:04:28,910 --> 00:04:31,990
What's the shape of the next block...?

38
00:04:32,190 --> 00:04:35,830
...Understand, think, and then act.

39
00:04:36,320 --> 00:04:40,300
Pro gamers process all of that in their brains at incredible speed.

40
00:04:40,630 --> 00:04:45,260
Then they rely on their reflexes to press the best buttons.

41
00:04:46,110 --> 00:04:49,180
Isn't it the same in football...?

42
00:04:49,570 --> 00:04:51,040
...I see.

43
00:04:52,950 --> 00:04:59,240
...In that moment, I... saw where the others were positioned... and what they were trying to do.

44
00:05:00,300 --> 00:05:07,350
...And I realized what weapons I had available... and knew where the ball would be lifted.

45
00:05:09,090 --> 00:05:12,290
...Because I was able to analyze it all at extremely high speed.

46
00:05:13,600 --> 00:05:17,120
...I was able to reach the shooting point faster than anyone!

47
00:05:17,340 --> 00:05:22,140
...That's true, but it happened because of your accumulated experience.

48
00:05:22,140 --> 00:05:25,050
...And while it appears to others that you suddenly did something amazing,

49
00:05:25,340 --> 00:05:30,390
the truth is your speed increased because your accumulated experience all focused into that one moment.

50
00:05:30,390 --> 00:05:35,730
So it's not a new skill he invented! It's an evolution.

51
00:05:35,730 --> 00:05:41,270
Exactly, like upgrading your cell network from 4G to 5G.

52
00:05:42,280 --> 00:05:44,710
...So that's what that feeling was.

53
00:05:46,130 --> 00:05:48,950
...That sensation of being so immersed I forgot myself...

54
00:05:49,740 --> 00:05:50,910
...Euphoria.

55
00:05:52,220 --> 00:05:57,060
...But I think I was able to do it... because the conditions were right.

56
00:05:57,630 --> 00:06:00,880
...Rin and Shidou were fighting each other, which made it easy to slip behind them.

57
00:06:01,320 --> 00:06:04,980
...And more importantly, having you two on the same team. Without you, I couldn't have done it.

58
00:06:04,980 --> 00:06:08,040
Really, thank you, Nanase, Hiori!

59
00:06:09,100 --> 00:06:14,640
...Well... to be honest, you were the only one I could keep up with, Isagi-san.

60
00:06:15,090 --> 00:06:16,140
What do you mean?

61
00:06:17,540 --> 00:06:19,780
...Forgive me if this sounds rude.

62
00:06:20,320 --> 00:06:26,090
...But Rin-kun and Shidou-san's movements were too hard for me to keep up with.

63
00:06:26,800 --> 00:06:31,790
But I felt that I could keep up with your movements, Isagi-san, even if barely!

64
00:06:32,160 --> 00:06:37,540
I see... But thanks to you, my options for building attacks expanded, so I didn't mind at all.

65
00:06:37,540 --> 00:06:39,940
In fact, you were a huge help!

66
00:06:39,940 --> 00:06:42,320
Hiori-san was amazing too!

67
00:06:42,720 --> 00:06:45,630
I just played like usual, nothing more, nothing less.

68
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:51,040
And by scoring that goal, Isagi-kun, you allowed Nanase-kun and me to prove ourselves!

69
00:06:51,040 --> 00:06:54,350
So I think the three of us all gave it our best.

70
00:06:54,820 --> 00:06:58,180
Yeah! I really gave it my all and I have no regrets.

71
00:06:58,180 --> 00:07:01,350
Me too! And now all that's left is to wait for the results.

72
00:07:02,590 --> 00:07:05,320
You both did well in the tryouts!

73
00:07:05,320 --> 00:07:07,560
Ouch~ That hurts.

74
00:07:08,180 --> 00:07:09,780
~Sorry.

75
00:07:10,310 --> 00:07:14,490
...I've discovered a new sensation... but I haven't fully mastered it yet.

76
00:07:18,040 --> 00:07:23,750
If I can increase my ability to enter that trance-like state... until I can use it freely...

77
00:07:25,100 --> 00:07:27,380
Then I'll be able to reach even greater heights!

78
00:07:27,920 --> 00:07:31,130
Isn't the next match about to start?

79
00:07:31,510 --> 00:07:33,170
The second match!!

80
00:07:47,540 --> 00:07:52,240
...I've gotten a little stronger since that moment you didn't choose me.

81
00:07:53,470 --> 00:07:57,410
...To catch up to you... I did everything it took to win.

82
00:07:57,780 --> 00:07:58,710
...But!

83
00:08:00,250 --> 00:08:02,290
You're still ahead of me despite all that.

84
00:08:03,540 --> 00:08:05,580
...So I'll prove it to you here and now.

85
00:08:07,340 --> 00:08:10,630
I'm the only one who has the right to be by your side!

86
00:08:11,410 --> 00:08:12,990
W-Whoa! They're faster than before now!

87
00:08:12,990 --> 00:08:14,010
...I'll keep watch.

88
00:08:14,690 --> 00:08:16,220
Number ten.

89
00:08:16,610 --> 00:08:18,180
To there, Nagi, right?

90
00:08:18,980 --> 00:08:21,730
...The type of pass and the timing you want.

91
00:08:22,250 --> 00:08:23,730
I know them best!

92
00:08:23,730 --> 00:08:25,100
...Nice pass.

93
00:08:25,440 --> 00:08:27,150
~No it's not.

94
00:08:28,090 --> 00:08:29,540
...W-What a giant.

95
00:08:29,540 --> 00:08:32,450
So that's Ishikari, the tallest player in high school football!

96
00:08:33,190 --> 00:08:35,110
~Too low for me.

97
00:08:35,110 --> 00:08:36,120
Whoa!

98
00:08:36,620 --> 00:08:37,820
It went right to him!

99
00:08:39,190 --> 00:08:40,790
Great! Let's launch the counter!

100
00:08:40,790 --> 00:08:43,250
Pass it, you lower-eyelash bastard!

101
00:08:45,670 --> 00:08:47,040
Use me, Rin!

102
00:08:47,320 --> 00:08:49,750
They call me the useful monk!

103
00:08:51,460 --> 00:08:56,170
I-It came...! A pass from the best player in the facility.

104
00:08:56,170 --> 00:09:01,060
N-Now I'm on my way to score a counter-attack side by side with number one!

105
00:09:01,330 --> 00:09:02,520
Stop right there, Igaguri!

106
00:09:02,840 --> 00:09:04,790
I'll turn you into a sterile monk!

107
00:09:05,410 --> 00:09:07,520
...Getting past him won't be easy.

108
00:09:08,690 --> 00:09:11,440
...And it's impossible for a pass to reach me in front of the goal.

109
00:09:11,640 --> 00:09:13,740
...This might be my chance to deliver an assist.

110
00:09:14,550 --> 00:09:16,030
So who should I pass to...?

111
00:09:16,330 --> 00:09:18,570
Which genius should I follow...?

112
00:09:19,290 --> 00:09:22,060
...I'm at a crossroads that will determine my destiny right now.

113
00:09:24,560 --> 00:09:28,820
Which genius will take me to the next stage...?

114
00:09:30,500 --> 00:09:32,020
What are you doing?!!!!

115
00:09:32,020 --> 00:09:34,320
Do you want me to smash your skull in, Igaguri?!!!!

116
00:09:34,950 --> 00:09:35,670
Namu!

117
00:09:36,920 --> 00:09:38,140
...Ah.

118
00:09:39,720 --> 00:09:42,060
I got scared and passed it to him.

119
00:09:43,350 --> 00:09:45,730
~This way, antenna guy.

120
00:09:45,730 --> 00:09:48,690
Damn! Trying to slip behind me, antenna freak...?

121
00:09:48,690 --> 00:09:50,150
...But still!

122
00:09:51,070 --> 00:09:53,030
~The ball is within my reach!

123
00:09:53,030 --> 00:09:54,720
...Incredible! How wonderful!

124
00:09:54,720 --> 00:09:57,030
You dog! Get out of our way!

125
00:09:59,430 --> 00:10:02,590
...Show us what you've got... number five.

126
00:10:13,170 --> 00:10:14,640
Drag scissors...?

127
00:10:14,990 --> 00:10:19,340
A skill that lets you manipulate your opponent's center of gravity and suddenly burst past them at full speed!

128
00:10:19,920 --> 00:10:21,260
His explosive speed is incredible!

129
00:10:21,700 --> 00:10:24,720
Is he treating the number one like a child in a one-on-one?

130
00:10:24,720 --> 00:10:27,460
...The foundation of football is one-on-one duels.

131
00:10:27,460 --> 00:10:31,610
And if I'm put in that situation... I can proudly say I'm the best in Japan.

132
00:10:32,090 --> 00:10:33,360
Interesting!

133
00:10:33,510 --> 00:10:35,360
Face me, glasses guy!

134
00:10:37,770 --> 00:10:38,780
...Yukimiya.

135
00:10:39,310 --> 00:10:44,120
Despite his appearance...! He's a skilled player who relies on his physicality and speed.

136
00:10:44,570 --> 00:10:49,000
...If we consider that Bachira gets past opponents with his creative dribbling...

137
00:10:49,380 --> 00:10:51,000
~This way, you idiot.

138
00:10:53,040 --> 00:10:57,460
...This guy relies on imposing his power and speed on opponents with his dribbling.

139
00:10:57,800 --> 00:11:01,180
...So this is the playstyle of number five, Yukimiya Kenyu.

140
00:11:01,580 --> 00:11:03,970
The Emperor of One-on-One Duels!

141
00:11:04,900 --> 00:11:07,380
We can't handle him one-on-one! Let's press him together, Ishikari!

142
00:11:07,380 --> 00:11:09,690
...I don't want to take orders from you.

143
00:11:10,200 --> 00:11:11,440
But I'll do it.

144
00:11:11,440 --> 00:11:12,850
Use me, Yukimiya!

145
00:11:13,150 --> 00:11:15,150
~No~ Not a chance.

146
00:11:15,960 --> 00:11:18,570
~Things resolve peacefully if I score.

147
00:11:20,260 --> 00:11:21,720
He's going to shoot from there...?

148
00:11:22,120 --> 00:11:24,490
...But...! There's no path to shoot!

149
00:11:26,830 --> 00:11:28,090
A misplaced shot!

150
00:11:29,090 --> 00:11:31,080
~I'm a pacifist.

151
00:11:33,210 --> 00:11:36,750
...What is this trajectory...? The ball is dropping fast while heading out!

152
00:11:37,470 --> 00:11:38,710
A spinning shot...?

153
00:11:39,350 --> 00:11:41,510
~I'll clear it away.

154
00:11:41,510 --> 00:11:43,680
Yessss! Nice!

155
00:11:43,680 --> 00:11:45,680
Huh? There's another player there...?

156
00:11:47,850 --> 00:11:48,810
...Whoa.

157
00:11:49,980 --> 00:11:51,060
How heavy.

158
00:11:52,130 --> 00:11:52,910
Nagi!!

159
00:11:53,350 --> 00:11:54,560
...So you managed to trap it.

160
00:11:56,640 --> 00:11:58,730
~You're not bad, number six.

161
00:12:02,550 --> 00:12:05,490
...Incredible chemistry between two of the best players here.

162
00:12:09,450 --> 00:12:13,380
...You're really not... the person I knew anymore.

163
00:12:14,390 --> 00:12:15,860
Sorry, glasses guy.

164
00:12:16,590 --> 00:12:17,750
~I guess I stole your goal.

165
00:12:25,260 --> 00:12:27,890
...I can't score a goal like that.

166
00:12:28,370 --> 00:12:30,890
...Finding the best spot to trap that shot.

167
00:12:31,400 --> 00:12:32,900
...That didn't come from cooperation between them.

168
00:12:32,900 --> 00:12:36,250
They simply played off each other, bringing out the best in themselves!

169
00:12:36,610 --> 00:12:38,690
Great trap, Nagi-kun!

170
00:12:38,960 --> 00:12:40,600
Great shot, glasses guy.

171
00:12:41,050 --> 00:12:43,160
...Let's go...

172
00:12:43,620 --> 00:12:44,620
Yukima.

173
00:12:45,860 --> 00:12:47,480
~Just Yuki is fine.

174
00:12:48,960 --> 00:12:50,770
...My current level can't compare to theirs.

175
00:12:51,950 --> 00:12:55,960
...I guess I'm no longer enough to satisfy you anymore, Nagi.

176
00:12:57,310 --> 00:12:59,070
And what's with that expression of enjoyment on your face?

177
00:13:00,400 --> 00:13:04,300
...You're completely different from when you'd reluctantly receive my passes.

178
00:13:04,760 --> 00:13:05,500
...Idiot.

179
00:13:12,080 --> 00:13:17,680
...It seems you really... aren't mine anymore after all.

180
00:13:21,230 --> 00:13:23,110
~Time to answer back.

181
00:13:23,110 --> 00:13:24,950
Move around me, you antenna freak.

182
00:13:24,950 --> 00:13:27,320
~Don't order me around, Rinrin.

183
00:13:27,320 --> 00:13:29,470
I'm free, I do whatever I want!

184
00:13:29,470 --> 00:13:32,740
Who are you calling Rinrin, you damn insect?!

185
00:13:33,290 --> 00:13:35,710
...The Top Six really are on another level.

186
00:13:36,610 --> 00:13:42,750
They possess weapons that exceed the highest average a normal player can reach through training!

187
00:13:43,140 --> 00:13:44,300
...As for me.

188
00:13:45,300 --> 00:13:47,610
...I'm a versatile all-rounder.

189
00:13:48,320 --> 00:13:52,310
And no matter how much I improve myself and polish my game... my limit will always be 99%.

190
00:13:52,790 --> 00:13:54,400
...With these abilities of mine.

191
00:13:55,060 --> 00:13:57,730
How can I possibly compete with the Top Six...?

192
00:13:59,310 --> 00:14:01,400
Pass to me, Rin!!

193
00:14:02,610 --> 00:14:05,570
...Nice one, number one... a wise decision.

194
00:14:05,570 --> 00:14:06,940
You're so tall!

195
00:14:06,940 --> 00:14:07,820
...There's another one.

196
00:14:08,060 --> 00:14:10,950
Those two towering giants... just like the World Trade Center!

197
00:14:10,950 --> 00:14:12,700
Damn! Can we even reach them?

198
00:14:14,260 --> 00:14:16,750
...Those monsters linked up together.

199
00:14:20,040 --> 00:14:25,010
You bastard... since the start of the attack, you've been targeting places far from me, haven't you?

200
00:14:26,170 --> 00:14:27,970
...I was just clearing space.

201
00:14:28,200 --> 00:14:30,320
...A pest like you needs to disappear.

202
00:14:30,320 --> 00:14:33,070
~I'd like to see you try, virus hunter.

203
00:14:35,850 --> 00:14:38,110
...Becoming the world's best forward.

204
00:14:38,800 --> 00:14:42,610
...That's the only thing... they want.

205
00:14:42,960 --> 00:14:46,290
...No... it's the only thing that excites them.

206
00:14:46,640 --> 00:14:48,030
Those idiots!

207
00:14:50,040 --> 00:14:51,230
...This pisses me off.

208
00:14:51,990 --> 00:14:53,030
Let's score the next goal!

209
00:14:54,760 --> 00:14:58,490
...That's exactly why... they shine so bright.

210
00:15:00,370 --> 00:15:01,540
...Unlike me.

211
00:15:02,800 --> 00:15:06,380
...Even if I lose here and go home... I'll still live a life of prosperity.

212
00:15:07,380 --> 00:15:10,590
You are my heir, Reo!

213
00:15:11,460 --> 00:15:13,010
What is it you want?

214
00:15:13,310 --> 00:15:15,720
You ranked first in the academy again!

215
00:15:15,720 --> 00:15:20,130
You'll attend a prestigious university, then become a successful businessman!

216
00:15:24,420 --> 00:15:26,610
No, forget that.

217
00:15:26,900 --> 00:15:29,740
You were born to surpass me.

218
00:15:30,240 --> 00:15:34,160
And only a select few can play football.

219
00:15:36,570 --> 00:15:38,410
And you are not one of them!

220
00:15:38,750 --> 00:15:40,370
I'm saying this for your own good!

221
00:15:40,620 --> 00:15:42,790
I'm telling you this for your own good!

222
00:15:43,400 --> 00:15:44,460
...For...

223
00:15:44,570 --> 00:15:45,840
...your own good.

224
00:15:51,390 --> 00:15:53,200
...This is such bullshit.

225
00:15:55,300 --> 00:15:58,420
...All that awaits me if I go back there is boredom.

226
00:16:00,120 --> 00:16:02,600
...Everything I truly want is right here.

227
00:16:03,810 --> 00:16:06,860
...No... it has to be here.

228
00:16:08,930 --> 00:16:12,110
...And if the fate of my dream is to fade away bitterly...

229
00:16:12,340 --> 00:16:14,480
...Then I'll give up everything.

230
00:16:17,050 --> 00:16:18,700
And become a complete idiot!

231
00:16:18,940 --> 00:16:20,160
Here we go!

232
00:16:20,160 --> 00:16:21,140
...I...

233
00:16:23,010 --> 00:16:25,670
Are you bad at two-on-ones, glasses guy?

234
00:16:25,670 --> 00:16:27,000
~You're not funny at all.

235
00:16:27,320 --> 00:16:28,380
Get the second balls!

236
00:16:29,840 --> 00:16:35,260
...If my limit is 99% no matter how hard I try...

237
00:16:36,080 --> 00:16:37,260
Bring it on!

238
00:16:38,080 --> 00:16:42,270
...If mastering every playstyle at a high level is my talent...

239
00:16:43,750 --> 00:16:48,150
Then I have to trust my talent and push forward with courage!

240
00:16:50,570 --> 00:16:52,450
A pass is coming into the penalty area!

241
00:16:52,450 --> 00:16:53,860
Watch out for the receiver!

242
00:16:54,160 --> 00:16:56,490
...I'm no longer a mediocre jack-of-all-trades.

243
00:16:56,850 --> 00:16:59,200
I'm the king and master of all the skills I possess!

244
00:16:59,730 --> 00:17:03,660
I'll go head-to-head with all of you using everything I've got!

245
00:17:04,790 --> 00:17:06,540
...Pass it, Reo...! Over here!

246
00:17:11,570 --> 00:17:13,920
...I won't pass it to you, Nagi!

247
00:17:13,940 --> 00:17:15,680
He won't... pass...?!

248
00:17:16,590 --> 00:17:17,140
He's going to shoot...?

249
00:17:17,490 --> 00:17:20,480
...Just like you've changed since coming to Blue Lock...

250
00:17:20,480 --> 00:17:23,390
...I'll also change into whatever color I want!!!

251
00:17:25,640 --> 00:17:28,110
It went off course! A misplaced shot!

252
00:17:28,500 --> 00:17:29,400
...This trajectory.

253
00:17:29,720 --> 00:17:31,360
...It resembles the trajectory of the previous shot!

254
00:17:39,260 --> 00:17:42,410
Is he serious?! Copying Yukimiya's shot right away?

255
00:17:45,550 --> 00:17:49,710
~~This will be my new playstyle... the Chameleon style.

256
00:17:53,530 --> 00:17:54,670
...Incredible.

257
00:17:55,600 --> 00:18:00,600
That goal of Reo's came from using every aspect of his ability to copy others' movements.

258
00:18:01,450 --> 00:18:06,450
...So that's the method Mikage Reo arrived at in order to survive in Blue Lock.

259
00:18:08,520 --> 00:18:11,600
Copying others' movements...? That's an unbeatable technique!

260
00:18:11,600 --> 00:18:14,190
...No, it's still just a copy in the end.

261
00:18:14,530 --> 00:18:20,160
And no matter how much he masters imitating others' skills, his imitation rate will cap at 99%.

262
00:18:21,150 --> 00:18:26,200
And if he faces someone who has mastered the original move at 100% or more, he won't win easily.

263
00:18:27,040 --> 00:18:32,170
...He's right... a copy is always inferior to the original.

264
00:18:32,380 --> 00:18:37,510
...Plus, things like speed and height are physical abilities that can't be copied!

265
00:18:38,170 --> 00:18:41,770
...And I can't think of how he'd deal with that.

266
00:18:42,370 --> 00:18:46,890
...Which means Reo's copying ability... is still a new skill under development.

267
00:18:56,720 --> 00:19:02,620
...Just as I thought... it wasn't something I could compete with the Top Six with yet.

268
00:19:03,760 --> 00:19:07,750
...But now I know what path I need to take to evolve.

269
00:19:08,670 --> 00:19:10,800
...We lost in the end, Reo.

270
00:19:12,870 --> 00:19:15,280
But you scored an incredible goal.

271
00:19:16,150 --> 00:19:21,460
The ability to copy a talented player's weapon just by seeing it is truly amazing... and it suits someone with your high level of skill!

272
00:19:27,520 --> 00:19:28,270
...But it's...

273
00:19:29,480 --> 00:19:30,860
...Still not enough.

274
00:19:31,770 --> 00:19:33,630
For the football you want to play, right?

275
00:19:35,670 --> 00:19:36,420
Yeah.

276
00:19:38,250 --> 00:19:41,400
...Then pay me no mind... look down on me and wait.

277
00:19:42,500 --> 00:19:45,770
...I'll become someone you'd want to chase after.

278
00:19:50,770 --> 00:19:51,660
Got it!

279
00:20:01,170 --> 00:20:05,370
...I'll never be satisfied... until I get what I want!

280
00:21:38,070 --> 00:21:41,530
Wow! Itoshi Sae-kun all by himself!

281
00:21:41,530 --> 00:21:44,110
Thank you for coming to the meeting!

282
00:21:44,110 --> 00:21:47,070
Pleased to meet you! You genius!

283
00:21:50,680 --> 00:21:53,870
Hey, Sae-chan! Don't just walk in without permission!

284
00:21:54,140 --> 00:21:57,080
And who's the calf and the round-headed guy?

285
00:21:57,830 --> 00:22:00,800
Th-They're! The federation president and the national team coach!

286
00:22:00,800 --> 00:22:02,570
Then this'll speed up our talk.

287
00:22:02,970 --> 00:22:06,880
I watched that video of the U-20 team.

288
00:22:07,100 --> 00:22:09,220
And in short, they're all trash!

289
00:22:10,180 --> 00:22:13,530
Especially the forwards, they're disgusting trash!

290
00:22:14,970 --> 00:22:20,060
I only accepted joining the team because I'd get to play against the Blue Lock group.

291
00:22:20,060 --> 00:22:24,220
...But I didn't know the national team's level was this weak... I'm pulling out of this farce.

292
00:22:25,640 --> 00:22:29,010
...Listen! When we called them disgusting trash,

293
00:22:27,170 --> 00:22:29,980
Did you just insult my team...?

294
00:22:29,980 --> 00:22:32,950
N-Now now! You're the elder here, Hoicchan!

295
00:22:32,950 --> 00:22:36,920
I-Itoshi Sae-kun! So the national team's forwards didn't appeal to you.

296
00:22:36,920 --> 00:22:40,050
Then it's no problem if you want someone else!

297
00:22:40,050 --> 00:22:43,060
Even if they're overage or retired!

298
00:22:43,870 --> 00:22:45,460
I can choose whoever I want, right?

299
00:22:45,460 --> 00:22:49,680
Yes! As long as they're Japanese! Even if it's Ramos or Kazu!

300
00:22:50,790 --> 00:22:51,700
...In that case.

301
00:22:53,240 --> 00:22:57,330
There's an idiot in Blue Lock I want to play alongside!

302
00:23:00,970 --> 00:23:03,630
Blue Lock: Additional Time!

303
00:23:07,690 --> 00:23:11,060
...You're kind of... like a sloth, Nagi-kun.

304
00:23:12,030 --> 00:23:14,710
~Really...? I don't see any resemblance at all.

305
00:23:14,710 --> 00:23:16,540
...Literally his brother.

306
00:23:17,050 --> 00:23:20,020
...But you, Yuki, look just like him.

307
00:23:20,420 --> 00:23:22,090
...The deranged tarsier.

308
00:23:22,090 --> 00:23:25,420
Excuse me...? Is it because I wear glasses...?

309
00:23:26,070 --> 00:23:29,890
If it's about glasses, Zantetsu, who you teamed up with before, wore them too, right?

310
00:23:30,430 --> 00:23:34,440
...No... Zantetsu doesn't remind me of the tarsier.

311
00:23:34,440 --> 00:23:37,270
I didn't compare you to it because you wear glasses...! That's way too shallow.

312
00:23:37,890 --> 00:23:40,130
Then what did you base the comparison on...?

313
00:23:40,130 --> 00:23:41,830
...O-Oh, I see.

314
00:23:41,830 --> 00:23:43,480
What about Reo-kun then?

315
00:23:44,650 --> 00:23:46,720
...A chameleon, I think.

316
00:23:46,720 --> 00:23:48,320
I get it!

317
00:23:48,320 --> 00:23:50,700
...Copy...! Copy!

318
00:23:50,700 --> 00:23:52,700
And Aryu-kun, doesn't he look like a stick insect?

319
00:23:52,700 --> 00:23:53,950
~Glam.

320
00:23:53,950 --> 00:23:55,700
Glam bug!

321
00:23:56,040 --> 00:23:57,670
...And Isagi kind of looks like...

322
00:23:58,050 --> 00:23:59,380
A rhinoceros beetle!

323
00:23:59,380 --> 00:24:00,550
You loser!

324
00:24:01,310 --> 00:24:02,710
Because of his hairstyle!

325
00:24:02,710 --> 00:24:04,850
And Barou is an alpha gorilla, I think.

326
00:24:04,850 --> 00:24:06,040
You fahool!

327
00:24:06,040 --> 00:24:08,050
His face really is almost like that!

328
00:24:08,050 --> 00:24:10,310
And Tokimitsu is a female gorilla.

329
00:24:10,310 --> 00:24:11,000
~Ooga.

330
00:24:11,000 --> 00:24:12,700
We've found the perfect mate for Barou-kun!

331
00:24:12,700 --> 00:24:13,890
Oho!

332
00:24:15,030 --> 00:24:17,530
Then what about Rin-kun?

333
00:24:18,930 --> 00:24:20,230
...He's.

334
00:24:22,850 --> 00:24:24,460
A slime monster...?

335
00:24:24,460 --> 00:24:26,130
...P-Poison! Poison!

336
00:24:26,130 --> 00:24:29,470
A creature born from a failed experiment?

337
00:24:29,470 --> 00:24:31,970
Yeah, the kind that poisons you if you touch it.

338
00:24:31,970 --> 00:24:34,030
...P-Poison! Poison!

339
00:24:34,340 --> 00:24:35,700
What do you mean, slime monster...?

340
00:24:36,280 --> 00:24:37,030
...Ah.

341
00:24:37,530 --> 00:24:39,970
Also, Isagi is not a rhinoceros beetle!

342
00:24:39,970 --> 00:24:43,540
Those two tufts make him a larva eaten by a bird!

343
00:24:43,540 --> 00:24:46,710
....I'm getting close to the best part you geniuuuus!

344
00:24:46,710 --> 00:24:48,540
That's right! You're correct!

345
00:24:48,540 --> 00:24:50,470
As expected of you, number one!

346
00:24:50,470 --> 00:24:52,140
...Let's stop this game.

347
00:24:52,140 --> 00:24:53,540
...The three of us are donkeys in this game.